{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/882081-larp-lores-do-you-use-them-for-your-games","id":882081,"title":"LARP Lores Do you use them for your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-04T12:21:03-07:00","id":882081,"title":"LARP Lores Do you use them for your games?","content":"The W20 tabletop game that i prepare is still in its early planning stages and i really disliked the way my players used occult as a &quot;catch it all&quot; knowledge in the V20 game i ran for them beforehand, which is why i plan to use a &quot;hard cap&quot; by using the lores that are used in the LARP games and limiting the usefulness of occult.<br /> <br /> Did other STs have similar problems and solved it differently? If you solved it differently were the results satisfying? <br /> <br /> While i was changing some of them (mainly the basic/intermediate/advanced stuff) i also found some pieces of information i am not even sure what they mean and look them up now. One of them was: <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;The purpose of the Spiral - to be revealed to a player who actually gains this level of lore.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is difficult for me to understand what exactly is meant here - is this a connection for a Wraith game and their labyrinth? Truth be told, i could just make something up for my players, but i would like to know if there are some &quot;official&quot; answers somewhere that i am not aware of or if there is some source list. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:33:39-07:00","id":882452,"title":"","content":"Do you have a link or page reference? My WAG is that an item card with a picture of a spiral on it is a note to the player that they should talk to a GM to see if they know what's on the card.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T20:22:24-07:00","id":882491,"title":"","content":"IME various Lore systems (I've seen a few of them) have been universally more bad than any good they do.<br /> <br /> What always seems to happen with them, is that instead of being niche Traits for restricting knowledge about in-depth secrets of groups the PC shouldn't know off hand, they build into a gigantic bookkeeping mess.<br /> <br /> I have had characters with more dots in Lores than <b>all their other Abilities combined</b>. Lore: Cosmology for general spirit knowledge. Lore: Wyrm/Weaver/Wyld for knowledge of triatic spirits (I've lost a character because Occult + Sense Wyrm wasn't &quot;enough&quot; to know had bad of a mess we walked into because it was ruled I didn't know how if it was a bane or just a tainted spirit without Wyrm Lore). Lore: Garou Nation to know things beyond the very basics. Lore: Sept (OK only once did I see this.. and I only played with that once) to know about the history of the Sept. Lore: every Tribe in your pack to understand their cultural stuff. Lore: Wraith and Dark Umbra because I was playing a Strider and needed to know about ghosts. Etc. etc. etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T21:39:34-07:00","id":882531,"title":"","content":"I actually hate the Lore systems in the MET as written. I do like the idea of having Lores as secondary skills just not having them as important as MET presents them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T00:17:01-07:00","id":882629,"title":"","content":"What would you change exactly? Give them out more freely and them being only support to occult or what would the direction be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:26:02-07:00","id":882671,"title":"","content":"There's been a few different versions of Lore out there. If you're planning on using one of the ones that work on a 0-5 scale, I think the most important thing is to never require Lores for things characters either belong to, or have a close relationship with; find other metrics if you don't want to let it all rest on Occult. Rank, Law, Rituals, Sept Standing, Totem, etc. are all traits you can use to figure out an &quot;effective Lore rating,&quot; for WtA to avoid bloating the game with Lores to gate off secrets.<br /> <br /> Second to that, try to keep Lores as general as possible. Lore: Vampires should generally be enough. Maybe Lore: [Sect] in a game with lots of crossover with vampires. Never get into Lore: [Clan/Bloodline] (with a small caveat that some essentially constitute Sects of their own) even in a heavily crossover game.<br /> <br /> Finally, when using Lores, never force players to buy Lores because they heard [Fact] about a subject. If a PC learns from experience that stakes only incapacitate vampires and they'll wake up when it is removed, don't make them buy Lore: Vampires, or give them free dots in it. Lores should be far too broad for that; consider it like forcing someone to buy Spanish as a language to understand what common American borrow words like &quot;cojones&quot; means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:13:24-07:00","id":882720,"title":"","content":"That is some great advise and i will make sure to incorporate it! Especially the last paragraph is actually pretty helpful as i was thinking about giving it out &quot;fairly&quot; freely in these cases, as i dont believe in &quot;buying&quot; Backgrounds with anything else than time spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}